## Step-by-Step Process Guide: Building a Dashboard

### Phase 1: Discovery & Requirements (1-2 hours)

```
Step 1: Identify Business Question
❓ What decision will this dashboard inform?
❓ Who is the user?
❓ What actions will they take?

Example:
Q: Should we invest more in region X?
User: VP of Sales
Action: Budget allocation decision

Step 2: List Key Metrics
Key decisions require key metrics

For sales dashboard:
- Sales trend (what's happening?)
- Target vs actual (how are we doing?)
- YoY comparison (context)
- Forecast (where are we heading?)
- Regional breakdown (where's the opportunity?)

Step 3: Identify Available Data
What data exists?
- Sales database (transaction level)
- Budget table (planned spend)
- Product hierarchy (category, subcategory)
- Calendar (for time dimensions)

Can you answer the questions with this data?
- Sales trend: ✓ (use transaction date)
- Forecast: ✓ (enough history for exponential smoothing)
- Budget vs actual: ✓ (have both tables)

Step 4: Sketch Dashboard Layout
Paper sketch before building

┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│   Sales Dashboard               │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  KPI: Total Sales | YoY Growth  │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  Filters: Region | Year | Cat   │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  Sales Trend (large, central)   │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  Regional Map | Top Products    │
└─────────────────────────────────┘

Step 5: Review with Stakeholders
Share sketch before development
- Confirm metrics
- Confirm data available
- Get sign-off on design
- Save changes requests for Phase 2
```

### Phase 2: Data Preparation (1-2 hours)

```
Step 1: Connect Data Source
File → New Data Source
- Select data source type
- Authentication
- Connection string
- Choose tables

Step 2: Validate Data Quality
- Check row counts
- Verify date ranges
- Look for null values
- Validate dimensions

Step 3: Create Data Source Calculations
Common pre-calculations:

// Create calculated fields
Profit = [Amount] - [Cost]
Profit Margin = [Profit] / [Amount]
Order Date Year = YEAR([Order Date])
Order Date Month = MONTH([Order Date])

Step 4: Define Aggregations
Set default aggregations:
- Amount → SUM (default behavior)
- Count → SUM
- Price → AVERAGE (unit price per record)

Step 5: Create Hierarchies
Drag fields in order:
Date: Year → Quarter → Month → Day
Geography: Country → State → City
Product: Category → Subcategory → Product

Step 6: Hide Unnecessary Fields
- Remove ID fields (customer ID, order ID)
- Remove technical fields
- Keep only business-relevant fields

Step 7: Create Extracts (if large data)
Large dataset (>100M rows)?
- Right-click data source → Extract
- Filters on extract (optional)
- Schedule refresh: Daily, hourly, etc
```

### Phase 3: Create Worksheets (2-3 hours)

```
Step 1: Create Main Metric Sheet
Purpose: Trend over time

Columns: [Month]
Rows: SUM([Sales])
Marks: Line chart

Step 2: Add Trend Line & Forecast
Right-click chart → Trend Line
Options:
- Type: Linear (straight), Exponential, etc
- Confidence level: 95%
- Show equation & R²

Forecast:
Analytics → Forecast
- Months ahead: 3, 6, 12
- Season: Auto-detect

Step 3: Create Geographic View
Purpose: Regional performance

Marks: Region (geographic field)
Chart type: Map or Symbol map
Color: SUM([Sales])
Size: SUM([Orders])
Detail: [Profit Margin]

Tooltip:
<Region>
Sales: <SUM([Sales])>
Orders: <COUNT([OrderID])>
Margin: <[Profit Margin]>%

Step 4: Create Detail Table
Purpose: Drill-down data

Rows: [Region], [Product]
Columns: [Sales], [Profit], [Orders], [Margin]
Sorting: Sales descending

Step 5: Create Summary Cards
Purpose: Key metrics

Each card is separate sheet:

Sheet 1 - Total Sales:
- Marks: Card (single value)
- Measure: SUM([Sales])
- Format: $1.2M

Sheet 2 - YoY Growth:
- Measure: ([Sales This Year] - [Sales Last Year]) / [Sales Last Year]
- Format: 12%
- Color: Green if positive, Red if negative

Sheet 3 - Target Attainment:
- Measure: SUM([Sales]) / [Sales Target]
- Format: 95%
- Condition: Color (red < 95%, yellow 95-100%, green > 100%)

Step 6: Add Interactivity to Worksheets
Select month on trend → All sheets update

- On trend sheet, click month value
- Dashboard filter → Pass to all sheets

Show filter:
Right-click month field → Show filter

Filter type: Single select dropdown
```

### Phase 4: Build Dashboard (1-2 hours)

```
Step 1: Create Dashboard
Dashboard → New Dashboard
Set size: Desktop (1024x768) or Full width

Step 2: Add Components Top to Bottom
Tiled layout (faster loading):
☑ Tiled container (recommended)
☐ Floating (more control, slower)

Step 3: Add KPI Row
Drag sheets:
- Total Sales card
- YoY Growth card
- Profit card
- Target Attainment card
- Avg Order card

Size: Auto (equal width)
Height: ~80px

Step 4: Add Filter Row
Drag sheets:
- Region filter
- Year dropdown
- Category filter
- Metric selector parameter

Step 5: Add Main Visualization
Drag trend sheet
Size: Full width, ~300px height
This is the hero visualization

Step 6: Add Secondary Visualizations
Two-column row:
- Left: Regional map (50%)
- Right: Top products (50%)
Height: 250px

Step 7: Add Detail Table
Full width at bottom
Height: 250px (scrolls if needed)

Step 8: Configure Filters
For each filter control:
- Right-click → Configure
- Dashboard filter
- Apply to: Trend sheet, Map sheet, Table sheet
- Exclude: KPI cards (use parameters instead)

Step 9: Add Dashboard Title
Insert text box at top
"Sales Executive Dashboard"

Step 10: Preview & Test
Click Play icon (Preview)
- Click filters: Do all sheets update?
- Click month on trend: Do other sheets filter?
- Hover on elements: Do tooltips show?
- Check formatting: Colors, sizes, alignment
```

### Phase 5: Optimization & Publishing (1 hour)

```
Step 1: Performance Optimization
Test with actual data

Slow dashboard?
❌ Too many worksheets
✓ Combine sheets where possible

❌ Complex calculations
✓ Pre-calculate in database

❌ Large extracts not filtered
✓ Extract with filters applied

❌ Many worksheets visible
✓ Hide sheets, show on demand via tabs

Step 2: Visual Polish
- Consistent color palette
- Readable fonts (11-14pt)
- Align elements (use dashboard grid)
- Remove clutter (unnecessary lines, borders)
- Add white space (breathing room)

Step 3: Add Description
Help → Workbook description
"This dashboard shows monthly sales, regional performance, 
and product trends. Use filters to focus on specific regions 
or time periods. Click month on trend to see detail by product."

Step 4: Test on Mobile
Dashboard → Device layouts
Create phone layout (1 column stack)
Create tablet layout (2 columns)

Step 5: Set Refresh Schedule (if extract)
Data source → Refresh
- Extract: Daily at 10pm
- or: Every 4 hours

Step 6: Publish to Server/Online
Workbook → Publish to Tableau Server
- Name: Sales Dashboard
- Project: Executive Dashboards
- Permissions: Editors can edit, Viewers can only view
- Subscriptions: Auto-email daily

Step 7: Communicate Launch
Email stakeholders:
Subject: "Sales Dashboard is Live"
"Click here to access [link]
Key features:
- Region filter
- Month-to-month comparison
- Product performance ranking
Contact for issues: [your contact]"

Step 8: Monitor Usage
Server → Usage tracking
- Who accesses? (adoption)
- When accessed? (usage patterns)
- Which sheets viewed? (engagement)
- Query performance? (speed)

Iterate based on usage!
```

