- Dashboard: Executive sales dashboard
- Users: 100 executives checking hourly
- Problem: Takes 45 seconds to load (target: 5 seconds)
- Impact: Executives skip dashboard, decisions made on incomplete data
```

**Step 1: Diagnosis (30 minutes)**

```
Measurements:
Dashboard → Performance Recorder
- Query time: 38 seconds (85% of total)
- Render time: 7 seconds (15% of total)

Bottleneck: Database query is slow!

Investigation:
□ Check data volume
  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM Sales
  → 500 million rows
  → Way too much for live query

□ Check what dashboard displays
  - Regional summary (4 regions)
  - Product summary (30 products)
  - Monthly trend (24 months)
  → Only needs aggregated data!

□ Check for missing indexes
  → No index on (RegionID, Date)
  → Queries doing full table scans

□ Check query generated
  → Joining to 5 tables
  → No WHERE clause (filtering after aggregation)

Root cause:
Querying full 500M rows live
Then aggregating in Tableau
Filtering to summary level
```

**Step 2: Solution Design (1 hour)**

```
Option A: Add Indexes (No - not enough improvement)
- Might reduce query to 30 seconds
- Still too slow

Option B: Redesign Query (No - can't change database)
- DBA said "can't change production queries"

Option C: Extract with Pre-Aggregation ✓ BEST
- Create extract at aggregated level
- Region × Product × Day = ~30K rows
- Refresh daily (good enough for executives)
- Query: < 0.5 seconds

Option D: Live Query with Filters Applied
- Add data source filter (last 3 years, not all history)
- Still 250M rows
- Still slow

→ Chose Option C: Extract with pre-aggregation
